Z||000000||charliefarmer||05-18-2001||07:33 PM||||i have an 87 GTfastback,after running 80 or85 for about 25 miles,my check engine light comes on,after i slow down,it goes off.it's not running hot,or giving any other indications.before i go to the shop,anybody know what's up with this?||||reg||5
Z||000001||PBJ||05-18-2001||08:30 PM||||You have a sensor that is giving a reading beyond a set value that you ecm is programmed to understand.  Quite likely it is you O2 sensor because with an O2 sensor error the engine light comes on into a trip, not at start up.  And is the most intermittent-I mean works today but not yesterday.  You really need to check and retrieve the code set in you ecm for diag.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bob Englert||05-18-2001||09:20 PM||||In my experience a check engine light coming on at highway cruising speed is often a 32 (EGR system).  On my blue GT it was the EGR solenoid that had failed.  Replaced the solenoid and the problem disappeared.<P>You should read the codes to see what is being stored in the ECM.  The Haynes manual gives a list of the codes.  The factory Helms manual has excellent diagnostics for each code.<P>Don't guess, read the code and see what the car is telling you!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
